[Music]  this was a tea dance designed to feel  like the 50s a time when this was in the  charts  [Music]  and when the queen came to the throne i  went with a friend we didn't have a  television of our own but everybody in  the street  went to one house  where they had hired a television for  the day  just to watch the queen  among barbara wall and her friends there  is much affection and admiration for  their monarch linda bodel feels very  lucky to have met the queen in the 80s  when linda was working in a primary  school and this little reception child  when the queen went through to her  classroom got up out of the chair and  went over to the queen  and she said where's your crown mom  and the queen said i just wear my crown  for state occasions she said this is a  special occasion but it's not a state  occasion and she was just so so happy  everyone was welcome on the dance floor  as long as you could doci doe or at  least try to and of course there was  plenty of cake  what do you think of the queen  i like  the queen  and  i like all of her hats  nine-year-old poppy chapman came with  her aunt patricia chapman a fan of  william and kate  i think they're quite modern they seem  to be listening to the change to what's  happening in the world in terms of  various social issues  which has not necessarily been the case  as far as i know  they came to honour the queen but  perhaps more importantly it was also a  chance to be together  some of the people celebrating and  socializing here today are care home  residents who've spent much of the past  two years unable to see family or  friends  this afternoon they got to dance with  waltzing in their wheelchairs  we do try and get people out as often as  possible but coming to something like  this they've been able to look forward  to it get dressed up ready and having a  lovely time  this crown crocheted by staff at a local  care home was worn with pride  and the band had even written their own  song for the occasion  far from the mall and the pageantry at  the palace it was a wonderful tribute by  one small town to the queen of england  becky kochel sky news matlock

